<title>BELGIUM: EU again proposes 30,000 tns US malt barley quota.</title>
<headline>EU again proposes 30,000 tns US malt barley quota.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission has resubmitted a proposal to open a 30,000-tonne reduced tariff quota for imports of U.S. malting barley, a European Commission official said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The proposal, which  will be discussed by EU farm ministers next week, would allow the import of U.S. malting barley at 50 percent of the full duty.</p>
<p>The Commission's original proposal was rejected by an EU trade committee on December 20 on the grounds that the EU already had too much malting barley.</p>
<p>The U.S. has complained about the EU's delay in opening the reduced tariff quota, which would compensate U.S. exporters for loss of Austrian, Swedish and Finnish markets after these countries joined the EU in 1995.</p>
</text>
